# Parameters for the Zilath release signing key.
#
#   gpg --batch --gen-key scripts/gpg-release-key.params
#
# gpg asks for the passphrase through pinentry. It is deliberately NOT in this file:
# a signing key whose passphrase lives next to it in a repository is not a secret.
#
# RSA 4096 rather than Ed25519: what matters for a release signature is that it verifies
# in whatever tool meets the artifact, years from now. RSA is boring and universal.
# Sign-only, no encryption subkey — this key has one job.
# Three years: signatures made while the key is valid stay valid afterwards, and an expired
# key fails the bundle BEFORE an upload, which is the right moment to find out.
#
# Change Name-Real and Name-Email before running. They go on a public keyserver and stay
# there; the values below are the project author's.
%echo Generating the Zilath release signing key
Key-Type: RSA
Key-Length: 4096
Key-Usage: sign
Name-Real: Matteo Pratesi
Name-Email: pratesi.matteo@gmail.com
Name-Comment: Zilath release signing
Expire-Date: 3y
%commit
%echo done
